	resent in the Front BOX gallery: “Cryptic Bodies\,” an exhibition of four 
	interdisciplinary Houston-based femme artists who work in sculpture\, coll
	age\, zines\, and socially engaged practices. As one excavates their layer
	ed work\, bodies are revealed\, both human\, non-human\, touching upon wom
	en’s health\, fragmentary memories\, and interconnected ecosystems and ide
	ntities. The exhibit in the Back gallery features Chris Ireland’s “Dead Le
	tter Office\,” which explores home\, memory\, and placelessness through ca
	refully constructed collages that combine fragments from lived experience\
	, online archives\, real estate listings\, and personal photographs. For “
	Mother Earth Weaves Infinite” in the Box 13 Window BOX Gallery\, Cathie Ka
	yser and Ellen H Ray use a variety of materials and techniques\, including
	 fabrics\, mulberry silks\, soft sculpture\, paper mache\, and wire and pa
	per sculptures to present an immersive experience that highlights the comp
	lexity of the mycorrhizal network. With this work\, the artists invite vie
	wers to consider the interconnectedness of all living systems. The Earth\,
	 and the universe encompassing it\, is a master plan of intelligent design
	 that holds lessons for us about systems that work. Moving to our Upstairs
	 BOX gallery we are excited to introduce “Grip Strength: An Army of Lovers
	 Shall Not Fail” by KT Abadir-Mullally. Through interactive soft sculpture
	s and ceramics inspired by strength sports and queer activism\, the exhibi
